WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.307
[MUSIC]

00:00:05.307 --> 00:00:09.520
I graduated college feeling
like a total boss lady.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:13.598
Club leadership, student government, and
let's not forget, one of those fancy

00:00:13.598 --> 00:00:15.120
management consulting jobs.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:16.351
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; You know them.

00:00:16.351 --> 00:00:21.311
[LAUGH] I walked across that stage at
graduation feeling ready to take on

00:00:21.311 --> 00:00:22.160
the world.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:28.453
Within a year though,
that confidence had disappeared.

00:00:28.453 --> 00:00:33.155
I watched as each one of my peers
got staffed on cool new projects,

00:00:33.155 --> 00:00:34.873
while I sat unstaffed.

00:00:36.414 --> 00:00:41.086
After each project interview that resulted
in no project offer, I asked myself,

00:00:41.086 --> 00:00:43.290
what's wrong with me?

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:45.470
Why don't they want you?

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:49.560
When I eventually did get staffed,
my manager was cold and critical.

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:54.976
I remember my heart beating as I
walked to his desk to ask a question,

00:00:54.976 --> 00:00:57.373
making myself small and unobtrusive.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.766
This timidity followed me
to my second project, but

00:01:01.766 --> 00:01:03.767
this one had a lot more
client interaction.

00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:08.550
And all of a sudden my feedback
read lacks executive presence.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:15.849
I internalize this feedback, but without
a mentor to show me how it was done,

00:01:15.849 --> 00:01:19.699
or somebody giving me guidance
on how to actually change.

00:01:19.699 --> 00:01:23.320
All I did was keep fixating on
the fact that I was inadequate.

00:01:26.069 --> 00:01:30.147
I didn't feel ready to take on my job,
much less the world anymore,

00:01:30.147 --> 00:01:31.660
my confidence was gone.

00:01:34.512 --> 00:01:35.558
That intrinsic,

00:01:35.558 --> 00:01:40.100
untouchable belief in myself that I had
started my career with had vanished.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.895
Replaced by fear that I wasn't enough,

00:01:42.895 --> 00:01:46.190
doubt that I had a future
in the business world.

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:51.363
And jealousy of everyone around me who
seemed to fit in and have it figured out.

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:59.113
My confidence stayed low,
even as my performance improved enough to

00:01:59.113 --> 00:02:03.497
get me here, to the GSB,
with all of you incredible people.

00:02:03.497 --> 00:02:07.875
During my MBA one year I stumbled across
some research that changed my own

00:02:07.875 --> 00:02:09.900
perspective on my experiences.

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:12.987
It turns out what I had gone through,

00:02:12.987 --> 00:02:15.724
starting my career with
relatively high confidence.

00:02:15.724 --> 00:02:19.920
And then losing it with time,
that's actually startlingly normal.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:27.735
Women enter the workforce with confidence
roughly equal to that of their male peers.

00:02:27.735 --> 00:02:30.975
With time men's confidence
remains steady but

00:02:30.975 --> 00:02:36.410
the number of women who believe they have
what it takes to succeed is cut in half.

00:02:38.323 --> 00:02:40.880
It's something called
the confidence cliff.

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:47.934
This phenomenon in which women actually
lose confidence once they've started work.

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:50.660
There's a lot of potential explanations.

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:54.636
Everything from a lack of female role
models and mentors in the workplace.

00:02:54.636 --> 00:02:58.450
Lessons taught to young girls about
what it means to be a good girl.

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:01.384
The transition from an educational
experience that's relatively

00:03:01.384 --> 00:03:02.263
straight forward.

00:03:02.263 --> 00:03:06.720
So work environment that's politically
fraught and which like favors like.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:13.149
All these factors and
more come together to trip women up

00:03:13.149 --> 00:03:16.493
until they have fallen off the cliff.

00:03:16.493 --> 00:03:19.892
And look, this isn't just something
happening out there to faceless,

00:03:19.892 --> 00:03:20.790
nameless people.

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:23.706
It happens here too.

00:03:23.706 --> 00:03:28.435
In fact, when I surveyed
the women in our community,

00:03:28.435 --> 00:03:36.149
almost 90% said that they had experienced
a moderate or big decline in confidence.

00:03:36.149 --> 00:03:37.384
90%.

00:03:37.384 --> 00:03:42.839
Okay, this sucks.
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:03:42.839 --> 00:03:45.314
&gt;&gt; We know that confidence is critical for

00:03:45.314 --> 00:03:46.450
success.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:49.930
Without it, women are less ambitious,
less impactful and

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:52.302
less likely to get that next promotion.

00:03:52.302 --> 00:03:56.640
But here's the thing,
when women lose, we all lose.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:00.856
Our organizations miss out on the talent
of half of our their talent pool,

00:04:00.856 --> 00:04:03.310
and our leadership becomes less diverse.

00:04:04.312 --> 00:04:08.120
With worse outcomes as a result.

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:11.498
But beyond the organizational impacts and

00:04:11.498 --> 00:04:16.530
the professional impact,
it also just feels really shitty.

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:22.222
I hate the feeling of doubting myself.

00:04:22.222 --> 00:04:24.817
I hate that in addition to doing my job,

00:04:24.817 --> 00:04:28.130
I'm also fighting this
battle with confidence.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:35.610
But more than anything,
I hate the thought of each new generation

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:43.036
of women falling off the same cliff that
we've been falling off for generations.

00:04:43.036 --> 00:04:45.044
This has to stop.

00:04:45.044 --> 00:04:51.720
For the class at 2018, 2019,
2020, 2021, 2022 and beyond.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:54.800
For them I'm standing up here today.

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:57.420
And I invite you to stand with me.

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:04.780
Look, right here in this room we have
the future business leaders of the world.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:08.383
And an awful lot of people who are going
to be managing teams in the next

00:05:08.383 --> 00:05:09.017
few years.

00:05:09.017 --> 00:05:10.291
When surveyed,

00:05:10.291 --> 00:05:16.860
every single one of the women said that
having a supportive manager or mentor.

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:22.223
Would have had a significant
impact on her confidence of those,

00:05:22.223 --> 00:05:26.107
half said that it would
even be game changing.

00:05:26.107 --> 00:05:30.240
You have the ability to be game changing
for the young woman on your team.

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:33.372
Don't be like my first manager,

00:05:33.372 --> 00:05:37.564
who didn't even see that I was falling off
the confidence cliff right in front him.

00:05:37.564 --> 00:05:40.430
Get to know that young woman on your team.

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:41.670
Take her out to coffee.

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:44.580
Mentor her or
introduce her to someone who can.

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:51.372
Realize that your sponsorship will be game
changing not just for others see her but

00:05:51.372 --> 00:05:56.253
for how she sees herself And

00:05:56.253 --> 00:06:00.348
look, all of your energy, effort and time
on this will pay back to you ten fold.

00:06:00.348 --> 00:06:03.898
Not only will you get a more
effective member of your team,

00:06:03.898 --> 00:06:07.890
but her loyalty to you will propel
you through the organization.

00:06:10.507 --> 00:06:13.471
I know that all of you are wonderful and
you're going to go out there and

00:06:13.471 --> 00:06:16.799
be incredible leaders who fight the
confidence cliff along with the women on

00:06:16.799 --> 00:06:17.379
your teams.

00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:23.857
But we've also gotta start
talking to the women themselves.

00:06:23.857 --> 00:06:26.855
Look, this is the group of
people who are so powerful, so

00:06:26.855 --> 00:06:29.110
confident when they start their careers.

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:35.908
We've gotta give them the tools and
insight they need to keep that confidence.

00:06:35.908 --> 00:06:38.949
So for all the women in this
room who might be trying to

00:06:38.949 --> 00:06:40.920
overcome the confidence cliff.

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:41.736
And even for

00:06:41.736 --> 00:06:47.786
the 21-year-olds on the other side of that
camera still feeling on top of the world.

00:06:47.786 --> 00:06:50.230
And about to start your first
big job in a few months.

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:53.914
You are powerful.

00:06:53.914 --> 00:06:55.760
You can take on the world.

00:06:57.390 --> 00:07:00.129
If I could give any advice
to my 21-year-old self

00:07:00.129 --> 00:07:02.503
as I walked across that
stage at graduation.

00:07:02.503 --> 00:07:03.600
This is what I would say.

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:07.377
First, find your mentor, and

00:07:07.377 --> 00:07:13.204
get advice on how to guide your particular
manager to be a better ally for you.

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:20.592
Second, don't fall into that same
critical thinking that I had

00:07:20.592 --> 00:07:23.244
during the first few years of my career.

00:07:23.244 --> 00:07:26.870
Instead see feedback as a opportunity for
growth.

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:30.915
I know, I know, feedback's a gift right?
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:07:30.915 --> 00:07:32.785
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH] But really though,

00:07:32.785 --> 00:07:37.886
now I realize that it was my fixed
mindset that meant that I internalized

00:07:37.886 --> 00:07:42.840
the feedback I was given as
an condonation of my potential.

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:45.376
And that's a blow to my confidence.

00:07:45.376 --> 00:07:49.842
Instead, practice growth mindset,
which is all about

00:07:49.842 --> 00:07:55.080
embracing your ability, and
even your imperative, to evolve.

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:58.960
And if that growth takes a while,
go easy on yourself

00:08:02.928 --> 00:08:06.460
And last, get your awareness up.

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:12.206
For me, just knowing the confidence cliff
was a thing made me, A, less guilty for

00:08:12.206 --> 00:08:17.054
experiencing it, but B,
more motivated to rebuild my confidence.

00:08:17.054 --> 00:08:20.050
I didn't want to be just another
stat about gender inequality.

00:08:21.490 --> 00:08:26.590
For you I hope knowing about the cliff
makes you more proactive and

00:08:26.590 --> 00:08:31.144
fighting it, but
also let's you know you're not alone.

00:08:31.144 --> 00:08:36.117
We're all fighting this together on
behalf of all the generations of

00:08:36.117 --> 00:08:38.870
women that we will bring up behind us.

00:08:41.351 --> 00:08:45.762
So overcome the confidence cliff and
go forward into the world.

00:08:45.762 --> 00:08:50.091
I believe in you,
now keep believing in yourself,

00:08:50.091 --> 00:08:54.996
thank you.
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

00:08:54.996 --> 00:08:59.130
[MUSIC]

